The attached image (Figure 1 from npj Vaccines, 2017) demonstrates that Nano-11 nanoparticles significantly enhance antibody responses to vaccine antigens, comparable to or exceeding aluminum hydroxide (AH) adjuvant. Mice immunized with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) alone showed minimal anti-rPA IgG titers. However, co-administration with various doses of Nano-11 (200, 50, and 12.5 µg) resulted in significantly elevated IgG titers, on par with higher doses of AH (200 and 50 µg). Importantly, Nano-11 maintained potent adjuvanticity even at a low dose of 12.5 µg, whereas AH at this dose showed a reduced effect, indicating Nano-11's superior immunopotentiation at lower concentrations.